---
import BlogArticle from "../../components/BlogArticle.astro";
---

<BlogArticle
	title="How to Resize a PAN Card Photo on Mobile Without an App"
	description="Resize a PAN card photo on your phone in a browser: choose an image, crop it, set the current required dimensions, and save the JPEG without installing an app."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/blogs/resize-pan-photo-on-mobile/"
	heading="How to resize a PAN card photo on mobile with no app needed"
	intro="You can prepare a PAN photo from a phone using a mobile browser. A separate app is not required: select a picture, set the crop and dimensions, then download and inspect the result."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Resize in your mobile browser</h2>
		<ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6">
			<li>Open the <a class="text-link" href="/#photo-tool">PAN card photo resizer</a> in a recent browser such as Chrome or Safari.</li>
			<li>Tap the image selector and choose a photo from your gallery, camera roll, or Files app. If taking a new photo, use even light and a plain background.</li>
			<li>Select Photograph mode and use the appropriate crop. Drag the crop area with touch controls, keeping the head and shoulders framed as the application requests.</li>
			<li>Set the dimensions and file format required by the live application. Portal rules may differ, so do not assume the same pixels or KB limit for every form.</li>
			<li>Download the JPEG and open your phone’s Files or Downloads app to confirm that it saved, has the expected file size, and looks clear.</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Save the image on iPhone or Android</h2>
		<p>
			On iPhone, the browser may show a download prompt or place the
			file in the Downloads folder in Files; use Share or Save Image
			if that option appears. On Android, the file is usually available
			in Downloads or in the browser’s download list. The exact menu
			depends on your browser and phone settings. Keep the original
			photo until you have opened the resized copy and confirmed it is
			correct.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Privacy and troubleshooting</h2>
		<p>
			This site processes the selected image in your browser; the
			resizer does not upload it to our server. If the page reloads,
			the download does not appear, or a very large photo causes the
			browser to slow down, try a smaller source copy or use a device
			with more available memory. Do not share a personal photo with a
			third-party service you do not trust.
		</p>
		<p>
			The <strong>nsdl photo resize</strong> tool can prepare a local
			image file, but current Form 93/94 requirements may not match
			older provider presets. Check the official application before
			uploading; resizing on mobile does not guarantee approval.
		</p>
	</section>
</BlogArticle>
